    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d253-a1">

                <pb facs="0419" n="323" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg323"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure No 1.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Lewis to Mr. Turner.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1871-10-23"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 23, 1871</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: By direction of the President I have to
                    inform you that on the night of the 22d instant a round of grape-shot was tired
                    into his mansion, and that a public meeting, held in this city this day, has
                    requested him to resign his office of President immediately.</p>
                <p>Your excellency will readily observe, without further remarks from me, that a
                    revolution exists in Liberia. I have, &amp;c., &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>JOHN LEWIS,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of
                        State.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
